// Global (loaded when a module converts to text an operand that may be a float: a float literal,
// `/`, `**`, `Math.*`, `as f32`/`as f64`, or a variable declared or initialized as one, inside a
// template's expression, `String(…)`, `.toString(…)` or `+` with a string; docs/internals/design/
// lazy-std.md "Float operands"): velt/lang/hooks/number_float, std's float printing, which
// lowering prefers to the runtime's. It names nothing a program can use.
// load for: a conversion operand may be a float
import "velt/lang/hooks/number_float";
